  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/b8d041c93422248311086d4f55289c92af383450</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/b8d041c93422248311086d4f55289c92af383450"/>
    <title>
        fix(kimi-for-coding): inherit attachment support for K3 models (#6102)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-04T23:27:03Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49832190?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>ysntony</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/ysntony</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix(kimi-for-coding): inherit attachment support for K3 models (#6102)

Both k3 and k3-256k inherit from the moonshotai/kimi-k3 lab base, which already declares attachment = true, so per the repo&amp;#39;s override-only rule the correct fix is to drop the stale attachment = false override rather than flip it.
On the Kimi For Coding endpoint both models accept image input (k3 also accepts video), per Kimi Code&amp;#39;s own subscription model catalog: k3 lists image_in and video_in, k3-256k lists image_in.
The declared [modalities] already match this (k3 inherits text/image/video from the base; k3-256k declares text/image), so the inherited flag is now consistent with modalities — same class of fix as #5793.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
